From: Roostr <noreply@roostr.space>
Subject: [PATCH] Kit adapter: store epochs as web_time::Instant so wasm32 builds

gpui-pre's executor clock (`cx.background_executor().now()`) returns
`web_time::Instant`. On native targets that is a re-export of
`std::time::Instant`, but on wasm32-unknown-unknown it is a distinct type, so
gpui-motion-kit 0.5.0 (with gpui-ce-motion 0.4.0) fails to compile for the
browser with 38x E0308 "expected std::time::Instant, found
web_time::time::instant::Instant".

- integrations/gpui-kit: every adapter epoch is a `web_time::Instant`
  (lib.rs Clock/MotionState/ValueState, layout, measured_size, pop_layout,
  reorder_native, scroll_native, shared_layout, vector, gesture_native);
  depends on web-time 1.
- core: re-exports `web_time::Instant` as `#[doc(hidden)] __Instant`, used by
  the `__motion_spatial_adapter` and `__motion_text_adapter` macros; depends
  on web-time 1. The CE-only `gpui` feature code is unchanged (it calls
  `Instant::now()` itself and is not built for the Kit adapter).

Nothing on the Kit path calls `Instant::now()`, spawns threads or reads
SystemTime, so with this change the adapter builds and runs in a browser
(checked: wasm32-unknown-unknown build, Chromium at 60 fps, reduced motion
snaps), and native behaviour is unchanged (web_time re-exports std there).
Cargo.lock files gain web-time (already a gpui-pre dependency).

Suggest adding `cargo check --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p gpui-motion-kit`
to CI.
---
diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index 34262ed..05bf7df 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@ native-tests = ["gpui", "gpui/test-support"]
 [dependencies]
 svgtypes = { version = "0.15.3", optional = true }
 unicode-segmentation = { version = "1.13.3", optional = true }
+web-time = "1"
 # Match the published CE API; no workspace patches or Git dependencies.
 gpui = { package = "gpui-ce", version = "=0.2.2", default-features = false, optional = true }
 
